<article class="prose-page" data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc><header class="prose-head" data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc><p class="pretitle" data-reveal data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc>Island guide</p><h1 class="h-big" data-reveal style="--delay:.1s" data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc>Larkspur Point</h1><p class="lead prose-lead" data-reveal style="--delay:.2s" data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc>The lighthouse, rocky shore and the deepest moorage.</p></header><img class="prose-img" src="<?php echo esc_url( get_theme_file_uri( 'assets/img/area-lighthouse.webp' ) ); ?>" alt="A red and white lighthouse on a cliff above the sea" width="1920" height="1072" loading="eager" decoding="async" data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc><div class="prose-body" data-astro-cid-h3xj43oc><p>Larkspur Point is a peninsula at the south end of Fennick Island, joined to it by a single causeway. Its rocky shore and deep water make it the place for boat owners.</p><p>Homes are few and change hands rarely. Most sales happen before they are listed, so tell me early if this is the place you want.</p><p>Wind is part of the deal. Houses here are built low, with storm shutters, and the gardens are grass and rock.</p><dl><dt>Ferry to the mainland</dt><dd>45 minutes via Fennick</dd><dt>Typical home</dt><dd>Waterfront house with deep-water moorage</dd><dt>Good for</dt><dd>Boat owners, people who like weather</dd></dl><button type="button" class="btn btn-solid" data-open-contact>Ask about Larkspur Point</button></div></article>
